      "blind_answer": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "Zn has a completely filled 3d10 shell both as the atom and as Zn2+. So, following NCERT, it is not regarded as a transition element."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u11_t00_2",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        3
      ],
      "blind_answer": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "Cr is an exception to the filling order: a half-filled 3d shell is extra stable, giving [Ar]3d5 4s1."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u11_t00_3",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        1
      ],
      "blind_answer": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "Fe is [Ar]3d6 4s2. Ionisation removes the two 4s electrons first, giving Fe2+ = [Ar]3d6."
    },
    {
